    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257">

                <pb facs="0488" n="414" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg414"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d257-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, [<date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-01-05">January 5,
                        1942</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. President</hi>:</p>
                <p>Please will you very kindly consider giving a few rationed carrots to the Dons to
                    help stave off trouble at Gibraltar? Every day we have the use of the harbour is
                    a gain, especially in view of some other ideas we have discussed. I am told it
                    only needs a word to Wallace.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d257-f2"/></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. C.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>5. 1. 42</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d257-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d257-f1-content">
                <p>The source text is on White House stationery; Churchill’s initials are typed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d257-f2" n="2" xml:id="d257-f2-content">
                <p>Vice President Wallace was Chairman of the Board of Economic Warfare. No direct
                    reply by Roosevelt has been found, but for related documentation, see “Concern
                    of the United States Over Maintenance of Neutrality by Spain”, <ref
                        target="frus1942v03#pg_248">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1942, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, pp. 248</ref> ff., and “Negotiations
                    Between the American Chargé at Tangier and the Spanish High Commissioner
                    Regarding Economic Aid to Spanish Zone of Morocco and Tangier”, <ref
                        target="frus1942v04#pg_439">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >iv</hi>, pp. 439</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
